  "story": "kerrigan cannot assume cg-ec2-mighty-role. But he can pass it and launch EC2, so he boots an instance carrying the admin role and reads its credentials from IMDS. Neither iam:PassRole nor ec2:RunInstances is alarming alone \u2014 the path exists because they are held together, which is exactly what a per-resource scanner cannot see. The AdministratorAccess record is what the collector now produces for an attached AWS-managed policy -- its document, not just its name. passrole-only is the control: same PassRole grant, no compute action, so no route -- neither by walking CAN_PASS_ROLE nor via an admin-equivalent claim.",
